From 4a44bdb269eaee890e1df1e983d5d5e7a4c81cfb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Senior Matthew <SeniorMatt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 01:30:35 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 13/32] kcm_spellchecking: Form page, languages first,
 dictionary model bound after the first frame
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Page type: Form (docs/page-design.md). Sonnet settings, config keys and defaults unchanged. Not built yet.

Moved / renamed:
- First section (untitled): Default Language, "Preferred Languages: Choose Languages…" (was "Configure Preferred Languages…",
  kcm_spellchecking/Configure-Preferred-Languages), and the language autodetect checkbox (moved up from Options, relabelled
  "Detect the language automatically"; settings-autodetectLanguage).
- Section "Checking" (was "Options"): "Check spelling automatically by default" (was "Automatic spell checking enabled by
  default"), "Skip words in all uppercase", "Skip run-together words".
- Section "Ignored Words": "Ignored Words: Edit Ignored Words…" (was "Configure Ignored Words…"; "Configure" says nothing).
- Both dialogs kept as they were (built only on click).
- Shell aliases (ia/layout.json) already cover spelling/dictionary/sonnet.
HIG ids: HIG-001/005 (order by use), HIG-057 (no Options/Advanced title), button labels end with an ellipsis when they open
something. Accessible.name on the combo box.

Speed cause: settings->dictionaryModel enumerates every Sonnet backend/dictionary and was bound to the ComboBox when the
page was created. It is now assigned with Qt.callLater after the first frame; currentIndex reads `count` so it follows the model.
Also nine Kirigami.FormEntry/FormGroup items replaced by plain rows. After numbers: pending, manager will measure.

Unconfirmed: whether the Sonnet::Settings constructor itself already loads backends (then the first-frame win is smaller);
needs a measurement. Markers added for the two unchanged dialog rows because strict mode needs them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
